From 0568da00950251858a3b32964d0e7768bbf944a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:16:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GStreamer][GBM] Video in an external-only DMA-BUF layout
 shows no picture

https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=331206

Reviewed by NOBODY (OOPS!).

GLDisplay::bufferFormatsForVideo() lists every modifier that
eglQueryDmaBufModifiersEXT() reports for the video formats, and
buildDMABufCaps() offers all of them to the decoder as DMA_DRM caps.
The compositor imports a YUV frame one plane at a time, as R8, GR88,
R16 or GR1616 images bound to GL_TEXTURE_2D, and an RGB frame as one
image bound the same way. EGL reports some modifiers as external-only,
which GL can sample only through GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES. Mesa's v3d
driver does so for the Broadcom SAND128 column layout that the
Raspberry Pi HEVC decoder writes. When a decoder negotiates such a
modifier, every plane import fails and the video shows no picture.

Offer a modifier for a video format only when EGL can sample every
format the frame is imported as, with that modifier, as a 2D texture.
A decoder producing an external-only layout then negotiates with
glupload, which imports it as an external texture and converts it.

* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLDisplay.cpp:
(WebCore::isModifierSampledAsTexture2D):
(WebCore::GLDisplay::bufferFormatsForVideo):
* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/texmap/coordinated/CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf.cpp:
(WebCore::CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf::allPlaneFormats):
* Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/texmap/coordinated/CoordinatedPlatformLayerBufferDMABuf.h:

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
